      {
        "slide": 4,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "a thin cream ring with a lit radius from a glowing hub, laid on a town of separate street-lamp points that ends just past the ring and frays into scattered farm lamps on dark prairie, seen obliquely from altitude at night",
        "visual_consequence": "With the headline covered, the frame reads as a measured circle drawn around one bright point, taking in nearly all of a town whose lights stop just outside it. Beyond the ring the land goes dark with a few farm lamps. Without labels, the image shows that the reach covers the whole town around the hub.",
        "weakness": "Both judge charges are cured at native size. The far rows are now separate dots with dark blocks between them, not merged streaks (r2c2 at x 0 to 1080, y 600 to 900). The town's far edge is ragged and fades into sparse lamps toward the horizon, with no straight rim anywhere across the frame (r2c1 and r2c2 at y 470 to 640). The hub glow is the brightest point after the ring (r2c2 at x 0 to 90, y 690 to 790). Minor items: rows nearest the camera on the left still read as continuous lit streaks because the points crowd in perspective (r2c1 at x 0 to 700, y 650 to 900). The lower third is mostly dark prairie with sparse lamps (r3c1, r3c2 below y 250), which is plausible and stays clear of the footer. No dark square sprite tiles were found in this render.",
