      {
        "slide": 9,
        "role": "close",
        "subject": "four pine survey stakes with pink flagging and a taut survey string closing an empty rectangle on a parking lot, with faded stripes, concrete wheel stops and a storm grate, in one lamp pool, with the Interstate 35 light line on the horizon under an empty sky",
        "visual_consequence": "With the headline covered, the frame reads as a plot staked out on a commercial parking lot beside a highway, not yet built, with nothing in the sky. The light line on the horizon gives the dark land between the lot and the road a distance, so the middle of the frame now reads as unlit ground at night rather than an empty slab.",
        "weakness": "None blocking. The pad is about 110 px higher, and all four stakes, the closed string, the stripes, the wheel stops and the grate stay in frame with contact shadows (r2c1, r2c2 at y 660 to 900; r3c1, r3c2). The highway sits clear of the dek. Its sodium pole heads diminish toward the right, and the traffic line under them is denser on the right (r2c1 at y 290 to 375, r2c2 at y 315 to 370). Minor items at native size: the pole heads have no visible shafts, so they float as glow dots; the traffic reads as a dotted line rather than a streak; and the land between the lot's edge and the highway is still a near-uniform navy about 300 px tall (r2c1 at y 380 to 680), so it relies on the light line for its depth. Carried over from last round: the wheel stops cast no visible shadow, the grate sits proud of the surface, and the near stake's long cast starts a few pixels short of its contact blob (r3c1 at x 845 to 870, y 405 to 415).",
